gned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-5)^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{f}^{″}(5)}{2}.\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt{x+4}=(x+4)^{1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+4)^{-1/2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}(x+4)^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(5)=-\\frac{1}{4}(5+4)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {9}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{108}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of $(x-5)^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{″}(5)}{2}=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{108})}{2}=-\\frac{1}{216}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292802 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292803 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1041 "field-1" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292802 13194139534516 true] [17592186292801 1110 #uuid "f1c6fd19-f68a-56d0-9740-1e84e5077eec" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292802 1034 "-\\frac{1}{216}" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534516 true] [17592186292802 1111 #uuid "06279d38-f8a5-5580-9ed3-66655a63965d" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292803 1034 "-\\frac{1}{108}" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292803 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534516 true] [17592186292803 1111 #uuid "1fdfa1b4-3f4b-51c5-9444-7b6f3b8eadb8" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292805 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292808 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292810 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1089 "q-362768" 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534516 true] [17592186292804 1100 "Find the second-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{2}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1+2x)$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{2}(x)